In \cite{Karoui-Souabni1}, the authors have proposed the following  scheme for the computation of the GPSWFs. In fact,   since  $\psi^{(\alpha)}_{n,c}\in L^2(I, \omega_{\alpha}),$ then its series expansion
with respect to the Jacobi polynomials basis is given by
\begin{equation}\label{expansion1}
\psi^{(\alpha)}_{n,c}(x) =\sum_{k\geq 0} \beta_k^n \widetilde P^{(\alpha,\alpha)}_k (x),\quad x\in [-1,1].
\end{equation}
Here, $\widetilde P^{(\alpha,\alpha)}_k$ denotes the normalized Jacobi polynomial of degree $k,$ given by
\begin{equation}\label{JacobiP}
\widetilde P^{(\alpha,\alpha)}_{k}(x)= \frac{1}{\sqrt{h_k}}P^{(\alpha,\alpha)}_k(x),\quad h_k=\frac{2^{2\alpha+1}\Gamma^2(k+\alpha+1)}{k!(2k+2\alpha+1)\Gamma(k+2\alpha+1)}.
\end{equation}
